# model = astrodust_MW_euv
# Size-integrated extinction, albedo and scattering asymmetry per H
# for the Hensley & Draine (2023) astrodust+PAH Milky-Way model,
# carried into the extreme ultraviolet.
#
# Model definition: Hensley & Draine (2023), ApJ 948, 55
#   (astrodust + PAH, Milky Way R_V = 3.1 fit).
# Size distribution: ../data/release/size_distribution.dat
# Optics:
#   0.0912 - 39810 um : random-orientation T-matrix Q table,
#     ../tmatrix/output/q_astrodust_P0.20_Fe0.00_1.400.dat
#     (oblate spheroid b/a = 1.4, porosity P = 0.20, f_Fe = 0)
#   below 0.0912 um   : Mie for the VOLUME-EQUIVALENT SPHERE on the
#     same Draine & Hensley (2021) dielectric function,
#     ../data/dielectric/index_DH21Ad_P0.20_0.00_1.400
#   PAH : charge-resolved DL07 absorption (neutral + cation mixed by
#     f_ion, a > 100 A fully ionized).  PAH scattering is negligible
#     (Rayleigh) and is not modelled, so the PAHs enter extinction
#     through absorption only and the astrodust grains carry all the
#     scattering and the asymmetry.
#
# Wavelength range:  1.001032E-04 -  3.981000E+04 um, 1719 points.
#   The floor is set by the DH21 astrodust dielectric function,
#   whose own table stops at  1.000032E-04 um; a shorter floor is refused,
#   because (n, k) would freeze at the boundary value there.
#
# How far to trust the EUV band of THIS model:
#   Above 0.0912 um the astrodust optics are the b/a = 1.4 spheroid
#   T-matrix solution.  Below it they are volume-equivalent-sphere Mie
#   on the same dielectric function.  That shape approximation costs
#   <= 1.5% per grain in the orientation-averaged extinction and
#   0.2 - 0.7% after the size integral, and converges to a CONSTANT
#   -2.08% in the large-particle limit: by Cauchy's theorem the
#   orientation-averaged projected area of a convex particle is S/4,
#   which for b/a = 1.4 is 2.12% larger than pi a_eff^2 of the
#   volume-equivalent sphere.
#   There is NO external reference for this band: the HD23 author
#   release (extinction.dat, scattering.dat) stops at 12.4 eV.
#   Above 21.4 eV (1/lambda = 17.25 um^-1) the DL07 PAH cross section
#   is zero by construction, so the carbonaceous absorption there is
#   entirely D03 graphite -- Mie on the Draine 2003 dielectric
#   functions, random-orientation 1/3 parallel + 2/3 perpendicular.
#
# Column order follows Draine's kext_albedo tables and MoCHII's
#   par%ion_dust_kext reader: the first four columns are
#   lambda, albedo, <cos>, C_ext/H, and a reader may stop there.
#   Draine's 5th column is K_abs [cm^2/g]; ours is C_abs/H [cm^2/H],
#   so no dust-mass normalization is folded into the first six
#   columns; K_abs is a separate trailing column instead.
#   A host running the Zubko model through an ionizing band needs
#   exactly such a file: that model has no EUV extension of its own
#   (its optics table IS the model definition), so the host reads the
#   ionizing-band optics from a curve file instead.
#
# SCOPE: these are size-integrated TRANSPORT optics, not a dust model.
#   There is no size-resolved Cabs(lambda, a), no grain enthalpy and no
#   Planck integral here, so stochastic heating and thermal emission
#   cannot be computed from this file.  A host that needs emission must
#   build the model (build_astrodust / build_dl07 / build_zubko /
#   build_from_files).  The builder reads this very curve back in, and
#   dust_extinction serves it on the model wavelength grid while
#   dust_emission supplies the re-emitted spectrum, so the absorbed
#   power and the emission refer to one and the same grain.
#
# Units: lambda micron; cross sections cm^2 per H nucleon;
#   albedo and <cos> dimensionless.
#
# K_abs [cm^2/g] = C_abs/H / (M_dust/N_H), M_dust/N_H =  1.184949E-26 g/H.
#   The dust mass per H is this model's own size distribution
#   weighted by the solid density of each grain material:
#   M_dust/N_H = sum_pop rho * sum_a (4/3) pi a^3 dn(a).
#   Densities: rho_Ad = 2.74, rho_PAH = 2.0 g/cm^3 (HD23 conventions).
#
#             lambda               albedo                <cos>              C_ext/H              C_abs/H              C_sca/H                K_abs
#           (micron)                                                       (cm^2/H)             (cm^2/H)             (cm^2/H)             (cm^2/g)
 1.001032295532E-004  6.337195205551E-001  9.999997678393E-001  1.015833334362E-024  3.720799207464E-025  6.437534136160E-025  3.140049506786E+001
 1.012661432217E-004  6.208112651820E-001  9.999997628118E-001  1.013269859581E-024  3.842205160839E-025  6.290493434975E-025  3.242506178797E+001
